### What this track proposes
This chore changes one mapping in the measure-guard spawn-route guard so the agent measure-spec-review uses the ra-quota spec-review role instead of strategy. Three parity copies of guards.ts change at line 204. Red adds mapping assertions and a spec-review route-decision test; Green applies the mapping change and runs parity checks and plugin tests. Two pre-merge gate scripts must exit zero, and known test failures stay recorded as tech debt.

### How the current system works, per this spec
The guard reads ROLE_OF_AGENT in guards.ts to map each measure agent to a ra-quota role, then checks the spawn model against the approved routes for that role. Today ROLE_OF_AGENT maps measure-spec-review to strategy, so spec-review spawns face the strategy route list even though ra-quota has a separate spec-review role. The same map exists in three parity copies under mods/measure-guard and the two plugins, and role-spawn tests cover other roles with the same pattern.

